{"path": "index.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-view="both" data-level="all">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的？</title>
<meta name="description" content="A bilingual (English / Simplified Chinese) three-level explanation of why the sky is blue, presented side by side.">
<style>
/* ============================================================
   Why Is the Sky Blue? — self-contained bilingual presentation
   No external resources: system fonts only, no CDN, no images.
   ============================================================ */

:root{
  --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue",
          "PingFang SC", "Hiragino Sans GB", "Microsoft YaHei", "Noto Sans CJK SC",
          "Source Han Sans SC", sans-serif;
  --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia,
           "Songti SC", "Noto Serif CJK SC", "Source Han Serif SC", serif;
  --math: "Cambria Math", "Latin Modern Math", "STIX Two Math", "Times New Roman", Georgia, serif;

  --fs: 17px;                 /* driven by the A- / A+ controls */
  --maxw: 1400px;
  --gap: 1.75rem;
  --radius: 14px;

  --bg: #f5f8fc;
  --bg-grad-1: #dceafd;
  --bg-grad-2: #f7fbff;
  --surface: #ffffff;
  --surface-2: #fbfdff;
  --border: #dde5ee;
  --border-strong: #c6d3e2;
  --text: #16202b;
  --text-soft: #4a5b6e;
  --muted: #7789 9c;
  --accent: #1668c7;
  --accent-soft: #e8f1fc;
  --accent-ink: #0b4b95;
  --zh: #a8341f;
  --zh-soft: #fceeea;
  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20,40,70,.05), 0 8px 24px -12px rgba(20,40,70,.18);
}

/* automatic dark mode */
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]){
    --bg:#0e1520; --bg-grad-1:#101c2e; --bg-grad-2:#0b1017;
    --surface:#141d2a; --surface-2:#18232f;
    --border:#25313f; --border-strong:#33455a;
    --text:#e7eef7; --text-soft:#a9bacd; --muted:#7f92a6;
    --accent:#5aa6f0; --accent-soft:#15263a; --accent-ink:#a8cdff;
    --zh:#f08a6e; --zh-soft:#2a1a16;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4), 0 10px 30px -14px rgba(0,0,0,.7);
  }
}
/* manual override */
:root[data-theme="dark"]{
  --bg:#0e1520; --bg-grad-1:#101c2e; --bg-grad-2:#0b1017;
  --surface:#141d2a; --surface-2:#18232f;
  --border:#25313f; --border-strong:#33455a;
  --text:#e7eef7; --text-soft:#a9bacd; --muted:#7f92a6;
  --accent:#5aa6f0; --accent-soft:#15263a; --accent-ink:#a8cdff;
  --zh:#f08a6e; --zh-soft:#2a1a16;
  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4), 0 10px 30px -14px rgba(0,0,0,.7);
}

*{box-sizing:border-box}
html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
body{
  margin:0;
  font-family:var(--sans);
  font-size:var(--fs);
  line-height:1.72;
  color:var(--text);
  background:
    radial-gradient(1200px 600px at 12% -8%, var(--bg-grad-1), transparent 60%),
    radial-gradient(1000px 500px at 95% 0%, var(--bg-grad-2), transparent 55%),
    var(--bg);
  background-attachment:fixed;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}

/* ---------- scroll progress ---------- */
#progress{
  position:fixed; inset:0 auto auto 0; height:3px; width:0%;
  background:linear-gradient(90deg,#2f8fe0,#7cc0ff); z-index:60;
  transition:width .08s linear;
}

/* ---------- toolbar ---------- */
header.bar{
  position:sticky; top:0; z-index:50;
  backdrop-filter:saturate(1.4) blur(10px);
  background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 86%, transparent);
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}
.bar-inner{
  max-width:var(--maxw); margin:0 auto; padding:.6rem clamp(.85rem,3vw,2rem);
  display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.6rem .9rem; align-items:center;
}
.brand{display:flex; align-items:baseline; gap:.55rem; margin-right:auto; min-width:0}
.brand .dot{width:.7rem;height:.7rem;border-radius:50%;
  background:linear-gradient(160deg,#7cc0ff,#1668c7); box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft); flex:none}
.brand b{font-size:1rem; letter-spacing:-.01em; white-space:nowrap}
.brand small{color:var(--muted); font-size:.78rem; white-space:nowrap}

.grp{display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.3rem; padding:.2rem;
  background:var(--surface-2); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:999px}
button{
  font:inherit; font-size:.8rem; font-weight:600; color:var(--text-soft);
  background:transparent; border:0; border-radius:999px;
  padding:.34rem .72rem; cursor:pointer; white-space:nowrap;
  transition:background .15s, color .15s, transform .05s;
}
button:hover{background:var(--accent-soft); color:var(--accent-ink)}
button:active{transform:translateY(1px)}
button[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--accent); color:#fff; box-shadow:inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.15)}
button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset:2px}
.hint{font-size:.72rem; color:var(--muted)}
kbd{font:600 .68rem/1 var(--sans); background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-bottom-width:2px; border-radius:5px; padding:.16rem .34rem; color:var(--text-soft)}

/* ---------- masthead ---------- */
.masthead{max-width:var(--maxw); margin:0 auto; padding:clamp(1.6rem,5vw,3.2rem) clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem) 0}
.masthead h1{
  font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.025em; line-height:1.15;
  font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.6vw,3.1rem); margin:0 0 .15rem;
}
.masthead h1 .zh-title{display:block; font-size:.62em; color:var(--zh); font-weight:600; margin-top:.25rem}
.masthead p.sub{color:var(--text-soft); max-width:64ch; margin:.55rem 0 0; font-size:.95rem}
.legend{display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.45rem; margin:1rem 0 0; padding:0; list-style:none}
.legend li{font-size:.74rem; color:var(--text-soft); background:var(--surface);
  border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:999px; padding:.22rem .62rem}

/* ---------- layout ---------- */
main{max-width:var(--maxw); margin:0 auto; padding:1.2rem clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem) 4rem}

.level{margin:2.6rem 0 0}
.level-head{
  display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:center; gap:.6rem .8rem;
  padding:.75rem 0 .6rem; border-bottom:2px solid var(--border-strong);
  position:sticky; top:3.1rem; z-index:20;
  background:linear-gradient(var(--bg) 62%, transparent);
}
.level-head .num{
  font:800 .72rem/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing:.11em; text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--accent-ink); background:var(--accent-soft);
  border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 26%, transparent);
  padding:.34rem .55rem; border-radius:7px;
}
.level-head hgroup{margin:0; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:baseline; gap:.5rem; min-width:0}
.level-head h2{font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.32rem; margin:0; letter-spacing:-.015em}
.level-head h2.zh-h{color:var(--zh); font-size:1.2rem}
.level-head .emoji{font-size:1.35rem; line-height:1}

/* parallel-text row: one subsection per row, EN | ZH */
.pair{
  display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);
  gap:var(--gap); padding:1.15rem 0; border-bottom:1px dashed var(--border);
}
.pair:last-child{border-bottom:0}
.cell{
  background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:var(--radius);
  padding:1.15rem 1.3rem 1.25rem; box-shadow:var(--shadow); min-width:0;
}
.cell.zh{border-left:3px solid var(--zh)}
.cell.en{border-left:3px solid var(--accent)}
.cell > :first-child{margin-top:0}
.cell > :last-child{margin-bottom:0}

.langtag{
  display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:.35rem;
  font:700 .66rem/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 .7rem;
}
.langtag::before{content:""; width:.5rem; height:.5rem; border-radius:2px; background:currentColor}
.cell.en .langtag{color:var(--accent)}
.cell.zh .langtag{color:var(--zh)}

.cell h3{
  font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.08rem; line-height:1.35; letter-spacing:-.01em;
  margin:0 0 .6rem; color:var(--text);
}
.cell h3::before{content:attr(data-num); color:var(--muted); font-family:var(--sans);
  font-size:.72rem; font-weight:700; margin-right:.5rem; letter-spacing:.05em}
.cell p{margin:.6rem 0}
.cell ul,.cell ol{margin:.6rem 0; padding-left:1.35rem}
.cell li{margin:.36rem 0}
.cell li::marker{color:var(--muted); font-weight:600}
.cell strong{font-weight:700}
.cell em{font-style:italic}
.cell .lead{
  font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.6;
  background:var(--accent-soft); border-radius:10px; padding:.7rem .9rem; color:var(--accent-ink);
}
.cell.zh .lead{background:var(--zh-soft); color:var(--zh)}
.term{font-weight:700}
.en .term{color:var(--accent-ink)}
.zh .term{color:var(--zh)}

/* tables */
table{border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:.85rem 0; font-size:.87rem}
caption{caption-side:top; text-align:left; font-size:.72rem; color:var(--muted); padding-bottom:.4rem}
th,td{border:1px solid var(--border); padding:.42rem .6rem; text-align:left}
thead th{background:var(--surface-2); font-weight:700; font-size:.76rem;
  text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; color:var(--text-soft)}
tbody tr:nth-child(even){background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-2) 60%, transparent)}
td.num{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; white-space:nowrap}

/* ---------- math (hand-built, no MathJax) ---------- */
.m{font-family:var(--math); font-style:normal; white-space:nowrap}
.m i{font-style:italic; font-family:var(--math)}
.m sub,.m sup{font-size:.72em; font-style:italic}
.m .up{font-style:normal}
.frac{display:inline-flex; flex-direction:column; vertical-align:-.42em;
  text-align:center; margin:0 .18em; line-height:1.18}
.frac > span{display:block; padding:0 .3em; font-size:.9em}
.frac > span:first-child{border-bottom:1.5px solid currentColor}
.par{display:inline-block; font-size:1.85em; font-weight:300; vertical-align:-.34em; transform:scaleY(1.06)}
.eq{
  display:block; margin:.9rem 0; padding:.75rem .5rem; text-align:center; overflow-x:auto;
  font-family:var(--math); font-size:1.06rem; line-height:2;
  background:var(--surface-2); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:10px;
}
.eq .m{font-size:1em}

/* ---------- view / filter visibility rules ---------- */
[data-view="en"] .zh, [data-view="en"] .zh-h, [data-view="en"] .cell.zh{display:none}
[data-view="zh"] .en, [data-view="zh"] .en-h, [data-view="zh"] .cell.en{display:none}
[data-view="en"] .pair, [data-view="zh"] .pair{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}

[data-level="1"] .level:not([data-level="1"]),
[data-level="2"] .level:not([data-level="2"]),
[data-level="3"] .level:not([data-level="3"]){display:none}
[data-level="all"] .only-single{display:none}
[data-level="1"] .level-head,[data-level="2"] .level-head,[data-level="3"] .level-head{top:3.1rem}

/* single-slide framing when one level is isolated */
[data-view="en"] .masthead h1 .zh-title,
[data-view="zh"] .masthead h1{display:inline}
[data-view="zh"] .masthead h1 .en-title{display:none}
[data-view="zh"] .masthead h1 .zh-title{display:block}

/* ---------- footer ---------- */
footer{
  max-width:var(--maxw); margin:0 auto; padding:1.5rem clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem) 3rem;
  border-top:1px solid var(--border); color:var(--muted); font-size:.78rem;
  display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.4rem 1.2rem; align-items:baseline;
}
footer code{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;
  background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:5px; padding:.05rem .32rem}

/* ---------- responsive ---------- */
@media (max-width: 900px){
  .pair{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); gap:.85rem}
  :root{--fs:16px}
  .brand small{display:none}
  .level-head{position:static}
}

/* ---------- print / projector ---------- */
@media print{
  header.bar,#progress,.hint{display:none !important}
  body{background:#fff; color:#000; font-size:11.5pt}
  .cell{box-shadow:none; border:1px solid #bbb; break-inside:avoid}
  .level{break-before:page}
  .eq{background:#f4f4f4}
  [data-view]{--view:both}
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
  html{scroll-behavior:auto}
  #progress{transition:none}
  button{transition:none}
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="progress" role="presentation"></div>

<header class="bar">
  <div class="bar-inner">
    <div class="brand">
      <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <b>Sky · Bilingual Deck</b>
      <small>EN / 中文 — side by side</small>
    </div>

    <div class="grp" role="group" aria-label="Language view / 语言">
      <button type="button" data-view="both" aria-pressed="true">Both 双语</button>
      <button type="button" data-view="en"   aria-pressed="false">EN only</button>
      <button type="button" data-view="zh"   aria-pressed="false">中文 only</button>
    </div>

    <div class="grp" role="group" aria-label="Audience level / 读者层级">
      <button type="button" data-level="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
      <button type="button" data-level="1"   aria-pressed="false">🧒 Kid</button>
      <button type="button" data-level="2"   aria-pressed="false">🎓 HS</button>
      <button type="button" data-level="3"   aria-pressed="false">🔬 PhD</button>
    </div>

    <div class="grp" role="group" aria-label="Text size / 字号">
      <button type="button" id="fs-down" aria-label="Decrease text size">A−</button>
      <button type="button" id="fs-up" aria-label="Increase text size">A+</button>
      <button type="button" id="theme" aria-label="Cycle theme">Theme</button>
      <button type="button" id="print" aria-label="Print or save as PDF">Print</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="masthead">
  <h1>
    <span class="en-title">Why Is the Sky Blue?</span>
    <span class="zh-title">天空为什么是蓝色的？</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="sub">
    Three explanations of the same phenomenon, pitched at increasing levels of depth —
    <span class="en">shown side by side with the Simplified Chinese translation</span>
    <span class="zh">（与简体中文译文并列对照）</span>.
  </p>
  <ul class="legend">
    <li>🧒 Level 1 · 3-year-old · 3 岁</li>
    <li>🎓 Level 2 · High school · 高中生</li>
    <li>🔬 Level 3 · Physics PhD · 物理学博士</li>
    <li>Keys: <kbd>1</kbd><kbd>2</kbd><kbd>3</kbd><kbd>0</kbd> levels · <kbd>E</kbd><kbd>C</kbd><kbd>B</kbd> language · <kbd>A</kbd><kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd> size · <kbd>P</kbd> print</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<main>

  <!-- ============================ LEVEL 1 ============================ -->
  <section class="level" data-level="1" aria-labelledby="l1-en">
    <div class="level-head">
      <span class="num">Level 1</span>
      <span class="emoji" aria-hidden="true">🧒</span>
      <hgroup>
        <h2 class="en" id="l1-en">For a 3-Year-Old</h2>
        <h2 class="zh zh-h" lang="zh-Hans">写给 3 岁的小朋友</h2>
      </hgroup>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <p class="lead"><strong>The sky is blue because sunlight is playing a game of hide-and-seek with the air.</strong></p>
        <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of lots of colors — like a rainbow! Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple are all hiding inside it.</p>
        <p>The air around the Earth is full of tiny, tiny bits — so small you can't see them. When sunlight zooms down through the air, it bumps into those tiny bits.</p>
        <p>The <strong>blue</strong> color bounces around the most. It gets knocked every which way and sprinkled all over the sky. The red color mostly just zooms straight through without bumping into anything.</p>
        <p>So when you look up, your eyes catch all the bouncy blue light that got knocked around. That's why the whole sky looks blue! 🌤️</p>
        <p><strong>At sunset</strong>, the light has to travel through <em>lots</em> more air to reach your eyes, and all the blue gets knocked away before it gets to you. What's left is the red and orange that didn't bounce. That's why sunsets are red! 🌅</p>
      </article>

      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <p class="lead"><strong>天空之所以是蓝色的，是因为阳光正在和空气玩捉迷藏。</strong></p>
        <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但其实它是由很多种颜色组成的——就像彩虹一样！红、橙、黄、绿、蓝、紫，全都藏在里面。</p>
        <p>地球周围的空气里挤满了极小极小的东西，小到你的眼睛根本看不见它们。当阳光飞快地穿过空气往下跑时，就会撞上这些小小的东西。</p>
        <p><strong>蓝色</strong>最喜欢到处乱蹦。它被撞得东飞西窜，撒满了整个天空。而红色呢，多半是直直地一路穿过去，几乎谁也没撞上。</p>
        <p>所以当你抬起头，眼睛里接住的全是被撞得乱跳的蓝光。这就是为什么整个天空看起来是蓝色的！🌤️</p>
        <p><strong>傍晚太阳落山时</strong>，光线要穿过<em>多得多</em>的空气才能跑到你眼睛里，蓝光在到达你之前就已经被撞跑了。留下来的，就是那些没怎么乱蹦的红色和橙色。这就是为什么晚霞是红色的！🌅</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ LEVEL 2 ============================ -->
  <section class="level" data-level="2" aria-labelledby="l2-en">
    <div class="level-head">
      <span class="num">Level 2</span>
      <span class="emoji" aria-hidden="true">🎓</span>
      <hgroup>
        <h2 class="en" id="l2-en">For a High School Student</h2>
        <h2 class="zh zh-h" lang="zh-Hans">写给高中生</h2>
      </hgroup>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <p class="lead"><strong>Short version: Rayleigh scattering.</strong></p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <p class="lead"><strong>一句话版本：瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）。</strong></p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.1">Sunlight is a mixture</h3>
        <p>Sunlight is electromagnetic radiation spanning the visible spectrum (~400–700 nm). The Sun's surface (~5,800 K) emits a near-blackbody spectrum that peaks in the green-yellow region, but our eyes integrate across all wavelengths and perceive the result as "white."</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.1">阳光是一种混合物</h3>
        <p>阳光是覆盖整个可见光谱（约 400–700 nm）的电磁辐射。太阳表面温度约 5,800 K，发出的光谱接近黑体辐射谱，峰值位于黄绿光波段；但我们的眼睛会对所有波长做积分，最终把它感知成"白色"。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.2">The atmosphere scatters light</h3>
        <p>When sunlight hits molecules in the atmosphere (mostly <span class="m">N<sub class="up">2</sub></span> and <span class="m">O<sub class="up">2</sub></span>, roughly 0.3–0.4 nm in size — far smaller than the wavelength of visible light), the oscillating electric field of the light drives the electrons in the molecule, turning each molecule into a tiny oscillating dipole that re-radiates light in all directions. This is <strong>elastic scattering</strong> — the light changes direction, not energy.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.2">大气会散射光</h3>
        <p>当阳光照射到大气中的分子（主要是 <span class="m">N<sub class="up">2</sub></span> 和 <span class="m">O<sub class="up">2</sub></span>，尺度约 0.3–0.4 nm——远小于可见光的波长）时，光的高频振荡电场会驱动分子内的电子，把每个分子变成一个微小的振荡电偶极子，向四面八方重新辐射光。这属于<strong>弹性散射</strong>——光只改变传播方向，不改变能量。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.3">The wavelength dependence is the key</h3>
        <p>Lord Rayleigh showed that for particles much smaller than the wavelength, the scattered intensity goes as:</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>I</i> ∝ <span class="frac"><span class="up">1</span><span><i>λ</i><sup>4</sup></span></span></span></div>
        <p>That fourth-power dependence is brutal. Compare blue vs. red light:</p>
        <table>
          <caption>Relative scattered intensity (∝ λ⁻⁴), normalised to green.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th>Color</th><th>Wavelength</th><th>Relative scattered intensity</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Violet</td><td class="num">400 nm</td><td class="num">~3.1×</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Blue</td><td class="num">470 nm</td><td class="num">~1.6×</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Green</td><td class="num">530 nm</td><td class="num">1.0× (baseline)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Red</td><td class="num">650 nm</td><td class="num">~0.44×</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Blue light (470 nm) scatters roughly <strong>4× more strongly</strong> than red (650 nm), and violet-to-deep-red spans nearly <strong>10×</strong> (<span class="m"><span class="up">(</span>700/400<span class="up">)</span><sup class="up">4</sup> ≈ 9.4</span>). So as direct sunlight passes overhead, the blue component gets scattered out of the beam and redistributed across the whole sky dome. The remaining direct beam looks slightly yellowish; the scattered light filling the sky looks blue.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.3">波长的依赖关系是关键</h3>
        <p>瑞利勋爵（Lord Rayleigh）证明：当粒子远小于波长时，散射强度满足</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>I</i> ∝ <span class="frac"><span class="up">1</span><span><i>λ</i><sup>4</sup></span></span></span></div>
        <p>这个四次方的依赖关系非常"残酷"。比较一下蓝光和红光：</p>
        <table>
          <caption>相对散射强度（∝ λ⁻⁴），以绿光为基准归一化。</caption>
          <thead><tr><th>颜色</th><th>波长</th><th>相对散射强度</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>紫光</td><td class="num">400 nm</td><td class="num">约 3.1 倍</td></tr>
            <tr><td>蓝光</td><td class="num">470 nm</td><td class="num">约 1.6 倍</td></tr>
            <tr><td>绿光</td><td class="num">530 nm</td><td class="num">1.0 倍（基准）</td></tr>
            <tr><td>红光</td><td class="num">650 nm</td><td class="num">约 0.44 倍</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>蓝光（470 nm）的散射强度约为红光（650 nm）的 <strong>4 倍</strong>；而从紫光到深红光，跨度接近 <strong>10 倍</strong>（<span class="m"><span class="up">(</span>700/400<span class="up">)</span><sup class="up">4</sup> ≈ 9.4</span>）。因此，当阳光直射过头顶时，蓝色成分被散射出原来的光束，并被重新分配到整个天穹上。剩下的直射光束看起来略微偏黄；而弥漫布满天空的散射光则呈现蓝色。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.4">Why not violet? (the classic follow-up question)</h3>
        <p>Violet scatters <em>even more</em> than blue, so why isn't the sky violet? Three reasons combine:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>The Sun emits <strong>less violet</strong> than blue in the first place (the blackbody curve falls off on the short-wavelength side).</li>
          <li>The upper atmosphere's <strong>ozone layer absorbs</strong> a chunk of violet and UV.</li>
          <li><strong>Human vision</strong> — our S-cones (short-wavelength) are less numerous and less sensitive at the violet end, and our brain interprets the mix as blue/cyan.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.4">那为什么不是紫色？（经典的追问）</h3>
        <p>紫光被散射得<em>比蓝光还强</em>，那天空为什么不是紫色？三个原因共同作用：</p>
        <ol>
          <li>太阳本身辐射的<strong>紫光就比蓝光少</strong>（黑体辐射曲线在短波一侧是下降的）。</li>
          <li>高层大气中的<strong>臭氧层会吸收</strong>掉相当一部分紫光与紫外光。</li>
          <li><strong>人眼的视觉特性</strong>——我们的 S 锥细胞（感短波）数量更少，且在紫端灵敏度更低，于是大脑把这种混合光解读成了蓝/青色系。</li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.5">Why sunsets are red</h3>
        <p>At sunset the Sun is near the horizon, so the light traverses up to ~38× more atmosphere than at zenith (the airmass scales roughly as 1/sin of the elevation angle). Over that long path, nearly all the blue and green is scattered out of the direct beam, leaving the transmitted reds and oranges. Additional <strong>Mie scattering</strong> from aerosols, dust, and water droplets (which is much less wavelength-dependent) enhances the glow.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.5">为什么晚霞是红色的</h3>
        <p>日落时太阳接近地平线，光线穿过的大气厚度可达天顶方向的约 38 倍（大气质量近似正比于仰角正弦的倒数，即 <span class="m">1/<span class="up">sin</span> <i>h</i></span>）。在这段漫长路径上，几乎所有蓝光和绿光都被散射出了直射光束，只剩下透射过来的红光与橙光。此外，气溶胶、尘埃和水滴带来的<strong>米氏散射（Mie scattering）</strong>对波长的依赖要弱得多，它会让这份霞光更加浓烈。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.6">Two things that keep the model honest</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Why clouds are white:</strong> Water droplets are ~1–10 µm, i.e. comparable to or larger than the wavelength (size parameter <span class="m"><i>x</i> = 2π<i>a</i>/<i>λ</i> ≳ 1</span>), so Rayleigh's <span class="m">λ<sup>−4</sup></span> law breaks down. Scattering becomes roughly wavelength-independent (<strong>Mie / non-selective scattering</strong>), so all colors scatter equally → white. Fog and milk use the same trick.</li>
          <li><strong>Why space is black:</strong> No air, no scatterers. Astronauts see a black sky even in daylight, because there's nothing to redirect light into their eyes from directions other than the Sun itself.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="2.6">两点帮助模型保持诚实的检验</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>云为什么是白色的：</strong>水滴直径约 1–10 µm，与光波长相当甚至更大（尺寸参数 <span class="m"><i>x</i> = 2π<i>a</i>/<i>λ</i> ≳ 1</span>），因此瑞利的 <span class="m">λ<sup>−4</sup></span> 定律失效。散射变得几乎与波长无关（<strong>米氏散射 / 非选择性散射</strong>），各色光被同等散射 → 呈现白色。雾和牛奶用的也是同一套原理。</li>
          <li><strong>太空为什么是黑的：</strong>没有空气，就没有散射体。宇航员即使在白昼也看到漆黑的天空，因为除了太阳本身所在的方向，没有任何东西能把光折进他们的眼睛。</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ LEVEL 3 ============================ -->
  <section class="level" data-level="3" aria-labelledby="l3-en">
    <div class="level-head">
      <span class="num">Level 3</span>
      <span class="emoji" aria-hidden="true">🔬</span>
      <hgroup>
        <h2 class="en" id="l3-en">For a Physics PhD</h2>
        <h2 class="zh zh-h" lang="zh-Hans">写给物理学博士</h2>
      </hgroup>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <p class="lead"><strong>The short answer is still Rayleigh scattering, but the honest answer requires several corrections.</strong></p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <p class="lead"><strong>简短答案仍然是瑞利散射，但诚实的答案需要若干处修正。</strong></p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.1">Starting point: dipole scattering from small particles</h3>
        <p>For a particle of radius <span class="m"><i>a</i> ≪ <i>λ</i></span>, in the electrostatic (dipole) limit, the polarizability is</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>α</i> = 4π<i>ε</i><sub>0</sub><i>a</i><sup>3</sup>
          <span class="frac"><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> − 1</span><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> + 2</span></span>,
          &nbsp;&nbsp;<i>m</i> = <span class="frac"><span><i>n</i><sub>particle</sub></span><span><i>n</i><sub>medium</sub></span></span></span></div>
        <p>and the total scattering cross-section is</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> =
          <span class="frac"><span><i>k</i><sup>4</sup></span><span>6π</span></span>
          <span class="par">(</span><span class="frac"><span><i>α</i></span><span>4π<i>ε</i><sub>0</sub></span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">2</sup>
          = <span class="frac"><span>8π</span><span>3</span></span> <i>k</i><sup>4</sup><i>a</i><sup>3</sup>
          <span class="par">(</span><span class="frac"><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> − 1</span><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> + 2</span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">2</sup></span></div>
        <p>giving the characteristic <span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> ∝ <i>λ</i><sup>−4</sup></span>. The differential cross-section carries the dipole radiation pattern,</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><span class="frac"><span><i>d</i><i>σ</i></span><span><i>d</i>Ω</span></span> ∝ (1 + <span class="up">cos</span><sup>2</sup><i>θ</i>)</span></div>
        <p>which is symmetric fore-aft. This predicts the observed ~90° <strong>linear polarization</strong> of skylight — first measured by Arago, and the working principle of Rayleigh's own sky-polarization compass and of insect navigation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.1">起点：小粒子的电偶极散射</h3>
        <p>对于半径 <span class="m"><i>a</i> ≪ <i>λ</i></span> 的粒子，在静电（偶极）近似下，其极化率为</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>α</i> = 4π<i>ε</i><sub>0</sub><i>a</i><sup>3</sup>
          <span class="frac"><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> − 1</span><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> + 2</span></span>,
          &nbsp;&nbsp;<i>m</i> = <span class="frac"><span><i>n</i><sub>particle</sub></span><span><i>n</i><sub>medium</sub></span></span></span></div>
        <p>总散射截面为</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> =
          <span class="frac"><span><i>k</i><sup>4</sup></span><span>6π</span></span>
          <span class="par">(</span><span class="frac"><span><i>α</i></span><span>4π<i>ε</i><sub>0</sub></span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">2</sup>
          = <span class="frac"><span>8π</span><span>3</span></span> <i>k</i><sup>4</sup><i>a</i><sup>3</sup>
          <span class="par">(</span><span class="frac"><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> − 1</span><span><i>m</i><sup>2</sup> + 2</span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">2</sup></span></div>
        <p>由此得到标志性的 <span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> ∝ <i>λ</i><sup>−4</sup></span>。微分截面带有偶极辐射的方向图样，</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><span class="frac"><span><i>d</i><i>σ</i></span><span><i>d</i>Ω</span></span> ∝ (1 + <span class="up">cos</span><sup>2</sup><i>θ</i>)</span></div>
        <p>它在前向与后向是对称的。这预言了天空光所观测到的约 90° <strong>线偏振</strong>——最早由 Arago 测得，也是瑞利自己发明的天空偏振罗盘以及昆虫导航机制的工作原理。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.2">Molecular vs. particulate: which regime are we in?</h3>
        <p>For air molecules the relevant quantity is not a geometric radius but the <strong>molecular polarizability volume</strong> <span class="m"><i>α</i>/4π<i>ε</i><sub>0</sub></span> (~1.74 Å³ for <span class="m">N<sub class="up">2</sub></span>, ~1.60 Å³ for <span class="m">O<sub class="up">2</sub></span>), or equivalently the refractive index. The Rayleigh scattering cross-section per molecule is</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> =
          <span class="frac"><span>24π<sup>3</sup></span><span><i>λ</i><sup>4</sup><i>N</i><sup>2</sup></span></span>
          <span class="par">(</span><span class="frac"><span><i>n</i><sup>2</sup> − 1</span><span><i>n</i><sup>2</sup> + 2</span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">2</sup>
          <span class="par">(</span>6 + <span class="frac"><span>3<i>δ</i></span><span>1 − <i>δ</i></span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">−1</sup></span></div>
        <p>where <span class="m"><i>N</i></span> is the number density and <span class="m"><i>δ</i></span> is the <strong>depolarization factor</strong> (<span class="m"><i>δ</i> ≈ 0.012</span> for <span class="m">N<sub class="up">2</sub></span>, <span class="m">≈ 0.050</span> for <span class="m">O<sub class="up">2</sub></span>), correcting for the anisotropy of the polarizability tensor. For air at 550 nm, <span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> ≈ 5×10<sup>−31</sup> m<sup>2</sup></span> per molecule and the sea-level volume scattering coefficient is <span class="m"><i>β</i> ≈ 1.1×10<sup>−5</sup> m<sup>−1</sup></span> — a scattering mean free path of order <strong>~90 km</strong> — long enough that the atmosphere is optically thin (<span class="m"><i>τ</i> ∼ 0.1</span> at zenith) and the sky is dark rather than uniformly glare-bright.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.2">分子散射还是颗粒散射：我们处在哪个区间？</h3>
        <p>对空气分子而言，相关的物理量不是几何半径，而是<strong>分子极化率体积</strong> <span class="m"><i>α</i>/4π<i>ε</i><sub>0</sub></span>（<span class="m">N<sub class="up">2</sub></span> 约 1.74 Å³，<span class="m">O<sub class="up">2</sub></span> 约 1.60 Å³），等价地也可以用折射率来表示。单个分子的瑞利散射截面为</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> =
          <span class="frac"><span>24π<sup>3</sup></span><span><i>λ</i><sup>4</sup><i>N</i><sup>2</sup></span></span>
          <span class="par">(</span><span class="frac"><span><i>n</i><sup>2</sup> − 1</span><span><i>n</i><sup>2</sup> + 2</span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">2</sup>
          <span class="par">(</span>6 + <span class="frac"><span>3<i>δ</i></span><span>1 − <i>δ</i></span></span><span class="par">)</span><sup class="up">−1</sup></span></div>
        <p>其中 <span class="m"><i>N</i></span> 是数密度，<span class="m"><i>δ</i></span> 是<strong>退偏振因子</strong>（<span class="m">N<sub class="up">2</sub></span> 约 0.012，<span class="m">O<sub class="up">2</sub></span> 约 0.050），用于修正极化率张量的各向异性。对 550 nm 的空气，<span class="m"><i>σ</i><sub>s</sub> ≈ 5×10<sup>−31</sup> m<sup>2</sup></span>（每个分子），海平面体散射系数为 <span class="m"><i>β</i> ≈ 1.1×10<sup>−5</sup> m<sup>−1</sup></span>——散射平均自由程量级约为 <strong>90 km</strong>——足够长，因而大气是光学薄的（天顶方向 <span class="m"><i>τ</i> ∼ 0.1</span>），天空是暗淡的蓝色，而非一片均匀的刺眼强光。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.3">Density fluctuations: the mechanism Einstein actually validated</h3>
        <p>A perfectly uniform, ideal gas would show <strong>no</strong> scattering — the forward amplitudes interfere destructively, and the fluctuation–dissipation theorem kills any excess. Scattering arises entirely from <strong>local density fluctuations</strong>, <span class="m"><i>I</i> ∝ ⟨Δ<i>ρ</i><sup>2</sup>⟩ ∝ <i>k</i><sub>B</sub><i>T</i><i>κ</i><sub>T</sub></span>. Einstein (1910) and Smoluchowski derived this, and the theory's spectacular confirmation is <strong>critical opalescence</strong>: as a fluid approaches its critical point, <span class="m"><i>κ</i><sub>T</sub> → ∞</span>, fluctuations grow to macroscopic scales, and the fluid turns milky. This is the same physics as the blue sky. Note the corollary: scattering is proportional to <em>density</em>, which is why the sky darkens toward black at altitude (fewer scatterers per unit volume) — the reason aircraft windows look almost space-black above the jet stream, and why the zenith is a deeper blue on a high mountain.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.3">密度涨落：爱因斯坦真正验证过的机制</h3>
        <p>一个完全均匀的理想气体<strong>不会</strong>有任何散射——前向的散射振幅相互相消干涉，而涨落–耗散定理也否定了任何多余的散射。散射完全源自<strong>局域密度涨落</strong>，<span class="m"><i>I</i> ∝ ⟨Δ<i>ρ</i><sup>2</sup>⟩ ∝ <i>k</i><sub>B</sub><i>T</i><i>κ</i><sub>T</sub></span>。爱因斯坦（1910 年）与 Smoluchowski 推导出了这一结果，而该理论最漂亮的验证就是<strong>临界乳光（critical opalescence）</strong>：当流体趋近临界点时，<span class="m"><i>κ</i><sub>T</sub> → ∞</span>，涨落增长到宏观尺度，流体变得乳白浑浊。这与蓝天是同一种物理。请注意一个推论：散射强度正比于<em>密度</em>，这正是天空在高海拔处向黑色变深的原因（单位体积内的散射体更少）——也是为什么在急流之上从飞机舷窗望出去近乎太空般的漆黑，以及为什么在高山上天顶的蓝更深。</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <article class="cell en">
        <p class="langtag">English</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.4">Radiative transfer and the observed color</h3>
        <p>What you actually perceive is a solution of the <strong>radiative transfer equation</strong>,</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><span class="frac"><span><i>dI</i><sub>ν</sub></span><span><i>ds</i></span></span> = −<i>κ</i><sub>ν</sub><i>I</i><sub>ν</sub> + <i>j</i><sub>ν</sub></span></div>
        <p>with a single-scattering source function that is the incident solar beam convolved with the <strong>phase function</strong>. Multiple scattering, ground albedo (a bright cloud deck or snowfield raises the sky's luminance and desaturates it), ozone absorption in the Chappuis band (450–750 nm, which actually <em>helps</em> push the zenith toward blue by removing red at long paths), and molecular (Rayleigh) plus aerosol (Mie) extinction all contribute.</p>
        <p>The <strong>aerosol optical depth</strong> <span class="m"><i>τ</i><sub>a</sub></span> dominates the visual character at most sites. Low <span class="m"><i>τ</i><sub>a</sub></span> (marine air, post-storm) → deep, saturated zenith blue. High <span class="m"><i>τ</i><sub>a</sub></span> (pollution, smoke, Saharan dust, post-Pinatubo) → forward-peaked Mie scattering washes the sky to milky pale blue and produces spectacular red sunsets. Volcanic stratospheric sulfate is exactly why 1816 was "the year without a summer" and why Turner's sunsets are so garish.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="cell zh" lang="zh-Hans">
        <p class="langtag">中文</p>
        <h3 data-num="3.4">辐射传输与所观测到的颜色</h3>
        <p>你实际感知到的，是<strong>辐射传输方程</strong>的一个解，</p>
        <div class="eq"><span class="m"><span class="frac"><span><i>dI</i><sub>ν</sub></span><span><i>ds</i></span></span> = −<i>κ</i><sub>ν</sub><i>I</i><sub>ν</sub> + <i>j</i><sub>ν</sub></span></div>
        <p>其单次散射源函数是入射太阳束与<strong>相函数（phase function）</strong>的卷积。多次散射、地表反照率（明亮的云层或雪原会抬高天空的亮度并使其饱和度下降）、臭氧在 Chappuis 波段的吸收（450–750 nm，在长路径下它通过移除红光，实际上<em>有助于</em>把天顶推向蓝色），以及分子（瑞利）与气溶胶（米氏）的消光，全都做出了贡献。</p>
        <p><strong>气溶胶光学厚度</strong> <span class="m"><i>τ</i><sub>a</sub></span> 在多数观测地点主导着天空的视觉特征。<span class="m"><i>τ</i><sub>a</sub></span> 低时（海洋空气、雨后）→ 天顶呈深邃饱和的蓝色。<span class="m"><i>τ</i><sub>a</sub></span> 高时（污染、烟霾、撒哈拉沙尘、皮纳图博火山喷发之后）→ 前向强化的米氏散射把天空冲淡成乳白浅蓝，同时造就壮丽的红色晚霞。火山喷发注入平流层的硫酸盐气溶胶，正是 1816 年成为"无夏之年"、以及透纳（Turner）笔下晚霞如此浓烈的原因。</p>
      </article>
